WEBVTT

00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:37.530
What is it that you like about Fujioka-kun?

00:01:43.310 --> 00:01:45.110
Sorry, Keiko.

00:01:45.110 --> 00:01:47.250
I was taken back because it was so sudden.

00:01:47.970 --> 00:01:50.750
You're right. I guess it was a bit sudden.

00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:53.140
What I like about him...

00:01:53.140 --> 00:01:56.860
Let's see... It began on the day of the entrance ceremony when...

00:01:56.860 --> 00:01:58.840
Oh no. Looks like this'll take a while.

00:02:00.110 --> 00:02:02.340
Wait, Kana!

00:02:03.370 --> 00:02:05.100
Aren't you forgetting something?

00:02:05.820 --> 00:02:06.480
Huh?

00:02:06.970 --> 00:02:08.190
Classroom cleanup.

00:02:10.290 --> 00:02:11.150
I'll leave things to you.

00:02:15.640 --> 00:02:18.740
Huh? My body feels numb all of a sudden.

00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:20.610
I must have caught a cold.

00:02:22.380 --> 00:02:24.190
Are you all right, Minami?

00:02:24.190 --> 00:02:29.210
I'm not feeling well, I'll leave the rest to you guys.

00:02:44.380 --> 00:02:48.640
What is it exactly? Is it Frasco or Francisco?

00:02:49.180 --> 00:02:50.190
It's Elastico.

00:02:50.580 --> 00:02:53.650
Oh well, who cares what the name is.

00:02:54.190 --> 00:02:59.900
Elastico is the name of the feint technique that's often used by South American soccer players.

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:02.810
I'm even more confused than before.

00:03:05.310 --> 00:03:06.370
Who is it?

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:09.250
Minami, how are you feeling?

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:10.580
Huh?

00:03:10.970 --> 00:03:12.610
Didn't you catch the cold?

00:03:13.690 --> 00:03:15.910
Oh yeah, I remember.

00:03:15.910 --> 00:03:17.550
That's right, a cold.

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:20.480
If it's about that, I've already recovered! I'm fine!

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:23.880
But since you're here anyway, come on in.

00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:26.580
Okay, then. Sorry to disturb.

00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:30.390
Wa–Wa–Wait... Fujioka!

00:03:44.380 --> 00:03:46.190
That's a girl's uniform.

00:03:46.190 --> 00:03:47.280
How cute.

00:03:59.730 --> 00:04:01.210
In the meantime, change into this.

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:10.350
Judging by Fujioka's reaction,

00:04:10.350 --> 00:04:14.180
he probably thinks that you're wearing Chiaki's clothes for some reason, right?

00:04:14.870 --> 00:04:17.310
You mean it? I wasn't exposed?

00:04:17.740 --> 00:04:18.900
I'm not too sure.

00:04:19.770 --> 00:04:24.150
Will I still be able to talk with Fujioka about the similarities between Churrasco and Elastico?

00:04:24.150 --> 00:04:28.160
I have absolutely no idea what you're talking about.

00:04:32.020 --> 00:04:33.160
I see.

00:04:36.270 --> 00:04:37.380
Leave it to me, Touma!

00:04:37.930 --> 00:04:41.660
I'll make up a reason why you're wearing a girl's uniform and get you out of this!

00:04:41.660 --> 00:04:43.310
Really?

00:04:43.310 --> 00:04:44.520
Yes, really!

00:04:45.310 --> 00:04:47.100
Hey! Fujioka!

00:05:03.080 --> 00:05:07.270
Touma, what are they doing in the other room?

00:05:07.270 --> 00:05:09.070
Who knows.

00:05:09.070 --> 00:05:10.700
Spare me please!

00:05:15.820 --> 00:05:19.170
Come, Fujioka! Just give up and put this on!

00:05:19.590 --> 00:05:20.910
I don't want to!

00:05:20.910 --> 00:05:25.110
Today's a day where my guests have to put on strange clothes for my amusement!

00:05:25.110 --> 00:05:26.800
I've never heard of such a thing!

00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:28.980
You've heard of it now, so put it on!

00:05:28.980 --> 00:05:30.020
I said no!

00:05:30.020 --> 00:05:31.270
Learn from Touma!

00:05:31.270 --> 00:05:32.510
I won't!

00:05:32.510 --> 00:05:34.570
Don't talk back! Just put it on!

00:05:34.570 --> 00:05:35.370
No, I won't wear it!

00:05:35.370 --> 00:05:36.690
It really suits you, Fujioka!
No, I won't wear it!

00:05:36.690 --> 00:05:37.960
It really suits you, Fujioka!

00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:40.680
I don't want to! Please spare me!
It really suits you, Fujioka!

00:05:40.680 --> 00:05:40.690
I don't want to! Please spare me!

00:05:48.750 --> 00:05:50.660
I'm home!

00:05:51.830 --> 00:05:54.780
Welcome back, Haruka-neesama.

00:05:54.780 --> 00:05:56.500
I'm home, Chiaki.

00:05:57.640 --> 00:05:59.490
Get up, Kana.

00:05:59.490 --> 00:06:02.420
Oh, w–welcome back...

00:06:02.420 --> 00:06:05.470
You'll catch a cold if you sleep in such a place.

00:06:05.470 --> 00:06:06.500
Okay...

00:06:10.910 --> 00:06:16.060
Oh yeah, tomorrow is the neighborhood cleaning day. I'll be counting on you two, okay?

00:06:16.450 --> 00:06:17.100
Okay.

00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:25.460
You have a cold?

00:06:25.460 --> 00:06:28.690
To be honest, I've had a slight fever since this morning.

00:06:29.790 --> 00:06:32.340
It looks like I caught a cold after all.

00:06:33.970 --> 00:06:36.120
It's because you were sleeping under the kotatsu.

00:06:36.120 --> 00:06:42.020
That's right. Hurry up and get some rest in bed. I'll make some okayu for you later.

00:06:42.020 --> 00:06:43.650
O–Okay...

00:07:00.830 --> 00:07:04.480
Sorry, I don't think I can help out with the neighborhood cleaning after all.

00:07:05.030 --> 00:07:07.210
Rest up for today.

00:07:08.910 --> 00:07:10.110
I'm sorry,

00:07:10.110 --> 00:07:16.270
I actually wanted to stay with you but there's no way I can avoid the neighborhood cleaning.

00:07:16.270 --> 00:07:18.500
I understand, Haruka-neesama.

00:07:18.950 --> 00:07:23.720
I'll have Chiaki stay by your side. If you need anything, just ask her, okay?

00:07:23.720 --> 00:07:25.300
Thanks.

00:07:36.810 --> 00:07:38.200
What's that?

00:07:38.200 --> 00:07:41.100
If you need something, just ring this bell.

00:07:41.100 --> 00:07:42.140
All right.

00:07:42.870 --> 00:07:45.030
Then, I'll be going.

00:07:45.030 --> 00:07:47.320
I'll be back this afternoon.

00:07:50.210 --> 00:07:54.660
Oh right, I think it'd be better for you to eat something light today.

00:07:55.260 --> 00:07:57.630
I can eat! I can eat!

00:07:57.630 --> 00:08:00.040
You see, I won't get better if I don't eat up.

00:08:00.750 --> 00:08:01.980
You're right.

00:08:01.980 --> 00:08:04.390
Then what would you like to eat for lunch?

00:08:04.390 --> 00:08:06.420
I'll make something you like.

00:08:06.930 --> 00:08:08.590
Really?

00:08:08.590 --> 00:08:12.840
Let's see... since the weather's pretty cold, nabeyaki udon might be good.

00:08:13.610 --> 00:08:14.900
Sure thing.

00:08:31.270 --> 00:08:32.400
What is it?

00:08:33.150 --> 00:08:34.740
Bring me some juice.

00:08:38.600 --> 00:08:40.450
Huh?

00:08:40.450 --> 00:08:42.360
What is it?

00:08:42.360 --> 00:08:47.300
Um, I'm thirsty. Can you get me a drink?

00:08:47.300 --> 00:08:48.210
All right.

00:08:49.840 --> 00:08:50.420
Here's your juice.

00:08:52.820 --> 00:08:54.070
Thanks.

00:08:56.610 --> 00:08:57.640
What?

00:08:57.640 --> 00:08:59.390
I'm done reading, next volume please.

00:09:02.440 --> 00:09:03.560
Here's the next volume.

00:09:04.180 --> 00:09:06.320
Thanks.

00:09:06.320 --> 00:09:07.930
I'm home.

00:09:09.050 --> 00:09:12.830
How do you feel now? Sorry I'm late.

00:09:12.830 --> 00:09:15.890
I'll make it right away, so wait a bit.

00:09:16.640 --> 00:09:18.280
Okay!

00:09:39.670 --> 00:09:40.930
Be careful, okay?

00:09:41.430 --> 00:09:42.140
Okay.

00:09:53.410 --> 00:09:55.070
It smells great!

00:09:55.660 --> 00:09:56.990
Kana...

00:09:57.570 --> 00:10:02.950
Is nabeyaki udon boiled or roasted? Which one?

00:10:03.720 --> 00:10:05.450
Enough talk! Just bring it over!

00:10:06.830 --> 00:10:08.840
Here I go!

00:10:20.060 --> 00:10:21.800
You were faking, weren't you?

00:10:28.560 --> 00:10:31.350
What are you saying?! Are you suspecting me?!

00:10:34.030 --> 00:10:38.960
You're not going to believe the words of your dear sister?

00:10:38.960 --> 00:10:40.820
Should I check your temperature for you?

00:10:46.450 --> 00:10:49.720
Right, I'll go get a thermometer.

00:10:49.720 --> 00:10:51.430
That's the only way to be accurate.

00:10:51.430 --> 00:10:52.210
W–Wait a minute!

00:10:56.090 --> 00:10:57.700
You traitor.

00:10:57.700 --> 00:11:03.260
All because you didn't want to go cleaning, you pretend to be sick to fool Haruka-neesama and I.

00:11:03.570 --> 00:11:09.390
T–That's not true! I really... do have a cold.

00:11:20.780 --> 00:11:22.280
How long do you plan on sleeping?

00:11:22.980 --> 00:11:26.900
It's Sunday. Let me sleep a bit longer.

00:11:26.900 --> 00:11:29.350
Have you forgotten today's plans?

00:11:30.880 --> 00:11:32.910
We're leaving you behind, you idiot.

00:11:34.000 --> 00:11:37.920
That's right. We're supposed to go shopping for spring clothes this afternoon,

00:11:37.920 --> 00:11:41.260
and then have all-you-can-eat galbi for dinner.

00:11:50.760 --> 00:11:51.890
It's hot...

00:11:52.320 --> 00:11:53.730
Don't tell me...

00:11:54.770 --> 00:11:57.830
I'm getting the chills all of a sudden.

00:11:57.830 --> 00:11:59.950
Don't tell me I really caught a cold.

00:12:02.940 --> 00:12:06.620
Who would have predicted this unbelievable turn of events?

00:12:06.980 --> 00:12:09.830
What to do? What should I do?

00:12:10.170 --> 00:12:15.630
If I tell them that I caught a cold, I don't know what Chiaki is going to say.

00:12:15.630 --> 00:12:19.090
I don't really care about shopping, but I do want to eat galbi.

00:12:19.470 --> 00:12:23.180
I seem to recall that all-you-can-eat galbi is for a limited time only.

00:12:23.180 --> 00:12:26.600
If I miss this chance, I don't know when it'll happen again!

00:12:27.670 --> 00:12:29.350
If I don't do something...

00:12:35.390 --> 00:12:36.550
Where's Kana?

00:12:36.550 --> 00:12:38.870
I think she's getting ready now.

00:12:40.090 --> 00:12:41.780
Umm...

00:12:43.910 --> 00:12:47.660
What's wrong? If you don't hurry and change, we're going to leave you behind.

00:12:48.800 --> 00:12:49.950
Just go without me.

00:12:52.310 --> 00:12:54.950
Actually I still have a lot of homework to finish.

00:12:54.950 --> 00:13:00.190
So, in order to fully enjoy the galbi tonight, I have to finish it up.

00:13:00.190 --> 00:13:01.700
Is that true?

00:13:01.700 --> 00:13:05.240
How rare of you to actually worry about homework.

00:13:06.070 --> 00:13:09.440
Well... I have to do it seriously once in a while.

00:13:09.440 --> 00:13:11.890
Besides, I want to eat some delicious galbi.

00:13:13.630 --> 00:13:15.310
Then about shopping...

00:13:15.550 --> 00:13:18.150
I'll leave that to you and Chiaki.

00:13:18.810 --> 00:13:20.110
I see...

00:13:20.550 --> 00:13:24.880
I'll finish up my homework before dinner. I'll leave the shop–

00:13:35.740 --> 00:13:38.270
The shopping problem has been taken care of.

00:13:38.270 --> 00:13:40.710
Next, I'll have to cure my cold before dinner.

00:13:47.270 --> 00:13:51.970
That's too bad. And here I thought the three of us could finally go shopping together.

00:13:51.970 --> 00:13:53.180
Yeah.

00:13:54.420 --> 00:13:56.470
What is it?

00:13:59.620 --> 00:14:01.230
Oh, good afternoon.

00:14:01.860 --> 00:14:04.070
Good afternoon.

00:14:04.070 --> 00:14:05.230
Are you doing shopping?

00:14:05.230 --> 00:14:06.980
Yeah.

00:14:06.980 --> 00:14:08.270
Oh, Minami-san.

00:14:08.270 --> 00:14:09.070
What?

00:14:09.600 --> 00:14:12.990
You're a member of the sports events committee, right?

00:14:13.530 --> 00:14:14.950
What about it?

00:14:15.290 --> 00:14:17.410
I'm in the committee too.

00:14:19.550 --> 00:14:20.840
That makes us colleagues.

00:14:21.740 --> 00:14:23.850
I'll see you at school then.

00:14:23.850 --> 00:14:25.170
Excuse me.

00:14:25.170 --> 00:14:26.900
Bye, Fuyuki-kun.

00:14:34.680 --> 00:14:40.480
Eh? Nobody's at home? It was Kana-chan who asked me to buy things for her.

00:14:41.560 --> 00:14:43.520
It's unlocked.

00:14:48.520 --> 00:14:49.820
Kana-chan?

00:14:52.370 --> 00:14:54.580
There's a pair of pincers under the kotatsu!

00:14:57.170 --> 00:14:59.370
What are you doing, Kana-chan?

00:15:01.420 --> 00:15:02.920
Oh, it's you, Uchida.

00:15:03.470 --> 00:15:04.540
What's wrong?

00:15:04.550 --> 00:15:08.960
I've been lying under the kotatsu every day, and before I knew it...

00:15:12.380 --> 00:15:13.820
I caught a cold.

00:15:15.100 --> 00:15:16.730
This is bad.

00:15:16.730 --> 00:15:19.000
You can't sleep under the kotatsu, you know.

00:15:19.000 --> 00:15:20.230
If you don't sleep in bed...

00:15:20.700 --> 00:15:26.270
No. You see... what's bad is that I already used the cold excuse yesterday.

00:15:29.900 --> 00:15:31.700
You were faking, weren't you?

00:15:32.290 --> 00:15:34.370
You traitor.

00:15:34.880 --> 00:15:40.160
All because you didn't want to go cleaning, you pretend to be sick to fool Haruka-neesama and I.

00:15:44.460 --> 00:15:47.040
Because of yesterday, I can't say I caught a cold again!

00:15:47.410 --> 00:15:52.480
Listen, Uchida! Don't tell anyone that I caught a cold...

00:15:52.480 --> 00:15:52.920
Are you okay?

00:15:56.500 --> 00:15:58.240
Sorry, sorry.

00:16:06.630 --> 00:16:08.690
I've brought the medicine you asked for.

00:16:09.350 --> 00:16:10.480
Same here.

00:16:24.380 --> 00:16:27.130
Thanks to you guys, I've replenished my nutrition!

00:16:27.480 --> 00:16:28.710
Next is you, Uchida!

00:16:28.710 --> 00:16:29.490
Yes!

00:16:29.490 --> 00:16:32.260
Bring me a blanket from my room.

00:16:32.590 --> 00:16:33.420
Yes!

00:16:37.010 --> 00:16:37.870
Mako-chan.

00:16:37.870 --> 00:16:38.300
Yes!

00:16:38.810 --> 00:16:43.060
Humidity is required to protect the throat. Bring me some hot water from the kitchen.

00:16:43.060 --> 00:16:44.100
Yes!

00:16:48.650 --> 00:16:50.580
That should do it.

00:16:50.580 --> 00:16:53.820
Next, I'll just switch the kotatsu's temperature to its highest.

00:16:59.290 --> 00:17:01.750
Is this really going to cure your cold?

00:17:01.750 --> 00:17:05.140
He's right. You should go to bed and rest instead.

00:17:05.140 --> 00:17:10.550
That won't work because I don't know when they'll be back.

00:17:10.550 --> 00:17:14.210
I have to look like I'm well at all times.

00:17:14.640 --> 00:17:15.910
Kana-chan...

00:17:15.910 --> 00:17:17.180
Be resolute.

00:17:18.440 --> 00:17:21.720
Be resolute. Be resolute.

00:17:27.650 --> 00:17:30.380
Isn't it great that the shopping went well?

00:17:30.380 --> 00:17:31.020
Yes.

00:17:31.490 --> 00:17:34.010
We bought some cute clothes for Kana as well.

00:17:34.010 --> 00:17:35.030
Now then...

00:17:35.790 --> 00:17:36.980
Getting hungry, right?

00:17:37.000 --> 00:17:40.450
Yes. I'm really looking forward to galbi.

00:17:40.900 --> 00:17:43.740
We have to indulge ourselves once in a while.

00:17:43.740 --> 00:17:46.880
I hope Kana finished her homework though...

00:17:46.880 --> 00:17:49.290
I think she's finished it for sure.

00:17:49.290 --> 00:17:50.680
You're right.

00:17:53.830 --> 00:17:58.470
For some reason, I feel worse than I did before...

00:17:59.050 --> 00:18:03.170
If I tell Chiaki that I have a cold again...

00:18:03.170 --> 00:18:06.990
I can't imagine how she'll scold me.

00:18:06.990 --> 00:18:09.480
It's frightening.

00:18:10.080 --> 00:18:12.670
At the very least, I have to pretend to be normal.

00:18:12.670 --> 00:18:14.980
How are you going to be normal?

00:18:17.380 --> 00:18:20.490
Well, when you're resting, you'd naturally lie down, right?

00:18:21.020 --> 00:18:24.110
And then, I'll slowly bury myself under the kotatsu...

00:18:24.110 --> 00:18:26.410
We're back!

00:18:28.550 --> 00:18:29.870
Sorry to disturb!

00:18:29.870 --> 00:18:31.880
Oh my, welcome!

00:18:36.380 --> 00:18:38.220
There's a pair of pincers...

00:18:38.700 --> 00:18:42.550
Kana, didn't I tell you that you'd catch a cold if you slept under the kotatsu?

00:18:43.200 --> 00:18:45.560
I won't catch a cold...

00:18:46.140 --> 00:18:47.970
Doesn't her voice sound a bit strange?

00:18:48.850 --> 00:18:51.970
That's because I've been under the kotatsu for so long...

00:18:51.970 --> 00:18:54.230
My throat became dry.

00:18:54.890 --> 00:18:57.190
Isn't she speaking kind of strange too?

00:18:57.860 --> 00:19:03.450
That's because I've been here too long and the heat is making me dizzy...

00:19:08.290 --> 00:19:11.030
I was under here the whole time, and I fell asleep–

00:19:11.030 --> 00:19:12.960
You caught a cold, didn't you?

00:19:33.250 --> 00:19:34.730
You caught a cold.

00:19:42.550 --> 00:19:43.490
It's so painful!

00:19:47.100 --> 00:19:49.490
There, there. It's going to be all right, go get some rest.

00:19:59.230 --> 00:20:01.830
It's so painful!

00:20:12.220 --> 00:20:15.090
Chiaki-sama! Where are you, Chiaki-sama?

00:20:16.870 --> 00:20:18.790
So you were here after all.

00:20:18.790 --> 00:20:20.240
This is <i>my</i> room, you know.

00:20:20.240 --> 00:20:23.530
I'm thinking of settling things with Fujioka once and for all.

00:20:23.530 --> 00:20:24.450
What's this all of a sudden?

00:20:24.900 --> 00:20:27.160
A peaceful and friendly way of settling it.

00:20:27.160 --> 00:20:29.410
Oh? That sounds good.

00:20:29.410 --> 00:20:35.420
I don't know where it came from, but I'm getting irritated with all of your banchou business.

00:20:35.910 --> 00:20:39.000
Fujioka won't bear his fangs in front of you and Haruka.

00:20:39.000 --> 00:20:42.130
That provided me with a hint to reconcile with him.

00:20:42.940 --> 00:20:45.380
Poor Fujioka...

00:20:45.380 --> 00:20:49.100
I wonder if his love will ever reach her...

00:20:50.190 --> 00:20:54.060
It should be about time for him to lose interest.

00:20:55.790 --> 00:20:58.940
I don't know how you plan on resolving this.

00:20:58.940 --> 00:21:04.220
But in case your ties were to worsen, I shall pass on to you the ultimate technique.

00:21:04.220 --> 00:21:08.780
However, use it only as a last resort.

00:21:13.270 --> 00:21:14.930
Hey, Fujioka!

00:21:17.010 --> 00:21:18.380
What is it, Minami?

00:21:19.120 --> 00:21:24.610
Why do you address Haruka and Chiaki by their names, but refer to me as Minami?

00:21:24.610 --> 00:21:25.050
Eh...

00:21:25.540 --> 00:21:28.190
Everyone in that place is known as Minami!

00:21:28.190 --> 00:21:30.350
So you can just call me Kana-chan!

00:21:32.380 --> 00:21:33.560
That's too embarrassing...

00:21:34.190 --> 00:21:36.520
Oh no, did he get angry?

00:21:36.520 --> 00:21:37.520
I guess there's no other way.

00:21:40.320 --> 00:21:42.150
Backdrop!

00:21:42.150 --> 00:21:45.100
I can't lift him...

00:21:48.640 --> 00:21:51.870
So that's how it is, I didn't use the technique you taught me.

00:21:52.520 --> 00:21:55.840
Our ties haven't worsened though.

00:21:55.840 --> 00:21:57.850
But he asked me, "What are you doing?"

00:21:57.850 --> 00:21:59.830
So you used it after all...

00:23:30.450 --> 00:23:32.680
Have you ever wondered why your beard becomes thicker after shaving?

00:23:32.680 --> 00:23:35.820
It only feels that way because the thick part of the roots become visible after you shave.

00:23:35.820 --> 00:23:40.060
However, when the hair grows back, only the surface of the beard has expanded.

00:23:40.060 --> 00:23:43.210
From a medical standpoint, neither the volume of hair nor the hair has changed.

00:23:43.210 --> 00:23:44.720
Therefore, you can shave without worrying!
